    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "principle_text",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 156,
      "width": 1660,
      "height": 98,
      "text": "\u2605  THE CORE PRINCIPLE  \u2605\nReasoning traces are the primary artifact; structured outputs are extracts.\nEach load-bearing decision is captured as multi-paragraph prose that walks through context, considers alternatives, and lands on a conclusion. Entities (people, storylines, biases, traits) appear as named subjects of sentences inside the reasoning \u2014 never as bulleted lists like 'characters: [marcus, ben]' or 'biases_invoked: [...]'. Structure (filenames, calendar ops, eval IDs) is the thinnest possible sidecar, generated AFTER the prose, never instead of it. The LLM does its hard work as reasoning; code extracts only where downstream consumers genuinely need structure.",
      "originalText": "\u2605  THE CORE PRINCIPLE  \u2605\nReasoning traces are the primary artifact; structured outputs are extracts.\nEach load-bearing decision is captured as multi-paragraph prose that walks through context, considers alternatives, and lands on a conclusion. Entities (people, storylines, biases, traits) appear as named subjects of sentences inside the reasoning \u2014 never as bulleted lists like 'characters: [marcus, ben]' or 'biases_invoked: [...]'. Structure (filenames, calendar ops, eval IDs) is the thinnest possible sidecar, generated AFTER the prose, never instead of it. The LLM does its hard work as reasoning; code extracts only where downstream consumers genuinely need structure.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 100007,
      "version": 1,
